              "help": {
                "text": "Correct the runner label or declare repository-specific labels in repository.runners."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "script-injection",
              "name": "ScriptInjection",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error",
                "enabled": true
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Detect untrusted values and secrets interpolated into scripts",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#script-injection"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Detect untrusted values and secrets interpolated into scripts."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#script-injection",
              "help": {
                "text": "Pass untrusted values through environment variables or action inputs. For secrets, prefer the tool's native environment variable or stdin over command arguments. GitHub secrets are automatically masked; register generated or fetched secrets with add-mask before use. Masking protects logs, not process arguments."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "script-interpolation",
              "name": "ScriptInterpolation",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error",
                "enabled": true
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Detect template values that may change script syntax",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#script-interpolation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Detect template values that may change script syntax. Unknown strings are checked independently of attacker control. Constrained, nonempty literal strings can be used as shell words; empty and all-decimal strings need a proved data-argument position. Booleans, numeric values, optional matrix members, numeric identifiers, SHA values, and hashFiles results also require that position."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#script-interpolation",
              "help": {
                "text": "Pass dynamic values through environment variables and read them as data in the script. Quoting a template expression does not prevent substitution before script parsing."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "shell-name",
              "name": "ShellName",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error",
                "enabled": true
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Validate script shells for the selected runner",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#shell-name"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Validate shell names for the selected runner and interpreter options supplied by built-in or plugin definitions. The rule cannot validate options when no interpreter definition matches or an argument contains an unresolved expression."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#shell-name",
              "help": {
                "text": "Select a supported interpreter, include {0} for the script filename in custom commands, and correct invalid options. Bash uses -o for set options and -O for shopt options."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "string-conditions",
              "name": "StringConditions",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error",
                "enabled": false
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Flag string conditions whose truthiness may be misleading",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#string-conditions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Flag string conditions whose truthiness may be misleading."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#string-conditions",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use a boolean expression; a nonempty string, including the string false, is truthy."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "syntax-check",
              "name": "SyntaxCheck",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error",
                "enabled": true
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Validate GitHub Actions workflow syntax",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#syntax-check"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Validate GitHub Actions workflow syntax."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#syntax-check",
              "help": {
                "text": "Check the indicated YAML field and its expected GitHub Actions value type."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "uncancellable-condition",
              "name": "UncancellableCondition",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error",
                "enabled": false
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Review jobs that can continue after cancellation",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#uncancellable-condition"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Opt-in policy for job conditions using always() that can evaluate to true during cancellation. Cleanup and cancellation notifications can require this behavior; the condition alone does not prove a mistake. Step conditions are not reported because action names do not establish whether their work is needed for cleanup. cancel-timeout-minutes does not force cancellation of a job whose condition keeps it running. Warning when enabled; --strict enables this policy as an error, including intentional uses."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#uncancellable-condition",
              "help": {
                "text": "If cancellation should stop the job, use !cancelled(). Keep always() when cancellation cleanup or reporting must run. A standalone always() offers a behavior-changing fix requiring explicit review; compound conditions have no replacement. See [GitHub's always() guidance](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/expressions#always) and the [job-versus-step cancellation test](https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/actions/runs/41520665123)."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "unsound-ternary",
              "name": "UnsoundTernary",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error",
                "enabled": true
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Report a \u0026\u0026 b || c expressions where b is always falsy",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#unsound-ternary"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Report a \u0026\u0026 b || c expressions where b is always falsy."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#unsound-ternary",
              "help": {
                "text": "The middle operand of a \u0026\u0026 b || c must be truthy to select b; use an explicit conditional or a truthy representation."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "unused-suppression",
              "name": "UnusedSuppression",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note",
                "enabled": true
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Report unused inline suppression selectors",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#unused-suppression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Report each inline suppression selector that matches no enabled findings in the checked YAML declaration. Information by default; errors with --strict. A selector used by any analyzed invocation of the same source is considered used. Incomplete analyses do not establish that a selector is unused."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#unused-suppression",
              "help": {
                "text": "Run actionlint fix --apply or use the editor quick fix to remove unused selectors. Selectors that suppress findings and the comment's reason are preserved. A suppression comment is removed when all its selectors are unused. Configure lint.rules.correctness.unused-suppression to change its level."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "vendor-lock-in",
              "name": "VendorLockIn",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error",
                "enabled": true
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Report repository URL references unsupported by GitHub",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#vendor-lock-in"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GitHub Actions accepts repository shorthand in uses. It does not accept full repository URLs. On the github execution target, report URL references in action steps and reusable-workflow calls. An HTTPS github.com URL offers a safe fix that removes its prefix while preserving the repository, action path and ref. Other hosts have no automatic substitution: the same owner/repository name on GitHub does not establish the same action. Docker registry URLs, local actions and dynamic references are excluded. Other execution targets are not restricted by this rule."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#vendor-lock-in",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use owner/repo[/path]@ref for an action hosted in the current GitHub instance. To use an externally hosted action, choose and verify a GitHub mirror, or check out the external source and invoke its local action. The prefix fix is unavailable for URLs with credentials, ports, URL encoding, queries, fragments or invalid shorthand."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "workflow-call",
              "name": "WorkflowCall",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error",
                "enabled": true
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Validate reusable workflow references and their declared inputs and outputs",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#workflow-call"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Check reusable workflow references and report missing or undeclared inputs and secrets using available local or remote metadata. Compare the caller's known token permissions with the called workflow's declared job permissions. Cache limits are checked for local calls. The expression-reference rule checks references to workflow outputs."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#workflow-call",
              "help": {
                "text": "Correct the reference and supply required inputs and secrets. For permission or cache conflicts, adjust the caller's grant or reduce the called workflow's requirements."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "workflow-command-syntax",
              "name": "WorkflowCommandSyntax",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning",
                "enabled": false
              },
              "properties": {
                "description": "Report malformed runner commands in literal script output",
                "queryURI": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#workflow-command-syntax"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The runner prints malformed or unknown :: commands as ordinary text. They do not create annotations or apply command effects.\n\nThis opt-in warning checks literal echo and printf output in Bash or POSIX shells, print calls in Python, and Write-Host, Write-Output or echo calls in PowerShell. It joins writes into stdout lines, including stop and resume tokens split across writes. Command processing is evaluated separately for each possible execution path. Comments and unused strings do not produce findings.\n\nRegistered interpreter settings and literal set changes determine errexit. Known failures and exit commands end execution. The check handles the errexit exceptions for conditions, negation and AND/OR lists. Unsupported commands, dynamic output, loops and complex control flow stop analysis of that path. A pending partial line is checked only at a known end of output. Python and PowerShell scripts are skipped entirely when a statement cannot be parsed by the limited literal-output model.\n\nThe rule is experimental because language coverage is partial and command-shaped text may be an intentional example. The syntax and case-insensitive extension list follow actions/runner revision 1ba885c2065fd9be317808ab3fd406f392635cf7, ActionCommand.cs and ActionCommandManager.cs. Extension-specific properties are not validated."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/kjanat/actionlint/blob/master/docs/rules.md#workflow-command-syntax",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use ::name::message or ::name key=value::message with a runner command name. Use stop-commands when intentionally printing command examples."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
